  "bodyHtml": "<p class=\"hw-prompt\">A company has $95,000 of notes payable outstanding. At year-end, $4,100 of interest has accrued but has not been paid or recorded. What effect will the adjusting entry have on net income?</p>\n      <select data-correct=\"Decrease net income by $4,100\"><option value=\"\">-- select --</option><option>Increase net income by $4,100</option><option>Decrease net income by $4,100</option><option>Decrease net income by $95,000</option><option>No effect on net income</option></select>",
  "notesHtml": "<ol><li>Accruing interest is an expense recognition: it decreases net income by the full accrued amount, $4,100, regardless of when the interest is actually paid.</li></ol><button class=\"answer-toggle\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Answer <span class=\"chev\">&#x2304;</span></button><div class=\"answer-reveal\"><ol><li>B. Decrease net income by $4,100</li></ol></div>"
